# Cloudflare Pages response headers (airhorn-kv7m). This file is copied verbatim into
# dist/ by `npm run build` (public/ is the Vite publicDir) and served by Cloudflare
# Pages on every response. It takes effect when the Pages deploy is the live origin;
# the current Google Frontend origin ignores it (the production switch is Paul's
# decision - see .github/workflows/deploy-pages.yml).
#
# Scope decision: these five are no-app-risk. The CSP is NOT here on purpose:
# index.html carries two deliberate inline scripts (the boot watchdog and the SW
# registration) plus one inline critical stylesheet, so script-src 'self' would
# break the boot - the CSP needs the inline-script decision first (external files
# vs hashes), tracked separately.
#
# Pinned by tests/pages-config.test.js - if you change a value, the pin names it.
/*
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=63072000; includeSubDomains; preload
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: geolocation=(), camera=(), microphone=(), payment=(), usb=()
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
